    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d434">

                <pb facs="0459" n="383" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg383"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.77–143</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of Division of Latin-American Affairs to Mr.
                        R. L. Farnham </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-09-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 28, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Farnham</hi>: Pursuant to our conversation
                    of yesterday, I take pleasure in transmitting herewith a copy of the French text
                    of the reply of the Minister of Haiti to the memorandum of the National Railway
                    Company of Haiti, regarding the differences now obtaining between the Government
                    and the railroad, together with a copy of the translation thereof.<anchor n="7"
                        xml:id="d434-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>As I have already informed you, we shall, upon receipt of advice from you, be
                    happy to arrange with Minister Ménos a date mutually satisfactory for the first
                    oral discussion of the points at issue, during which the Department will, of
                    course, be happy to lend its good offices.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Butler Wright</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d434-f1" n="7" xml:id="d434-f1-content">
                <p>Printed ante, inclosure to note from the Minister of Haiti, dated September 21,
                    1916, <ref target="#pg379">p. 379</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
